{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll      =         long long;\nusing ldbl    =       long double;\nusing ratio_t =       pair<ll,ll>;\nusing ratios  = multiset<ratio_t>;\n\nll b, c, g, n, q, r, t, u, x, y, z; map<ldbl,ratios> result;\n\nint main()\n{\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false), cin.tie(nullptr), cout.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cin >> x >> y >> n, g = gcd(x,y), x /= g, y /= g, q = x/y, r = x%y;\n\n    const auto save_ratio = [](ll a)\n    {\n        g = gcd(a,b), result[ldbl(abs(u-a*z))/t].emplace(b/g,a/g);\n    };\n\n    for (b = 1; b <= n; ++b)\n    {\n        g = gcd(y,b), c = b/g, z = y/g, t = b*z, u = q*t+r*c, save_ratio(u/z);\n\n        if (u%z)\n            save_ratio((u+z-1)/z);\n    }\n\n    auto p = result.cbegin()->second.cbegin();\n\n    cout << p->second << '/' << p->first;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long gcd(long a, long b) {\n        if (b == 0) return a;\n        return gcd(b, a % b);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out)));\n\n        String[] tokens = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        long x = Long.parseLong(tokens[0]);\n        long y = Long.parseLong(tokens[1]);\n        long n = Long.parseLong(tokens[2]);\n\n        long g = gcd(x, y);\n        x /= g;\n        y /= g;\n        long q = x / y;\n        long r = x % y;\n\n        // Using TreeMap with Double as key (similar to map<ldbl, ratios>)\n        TreeMap<Double, TreeSet<long[]>> result = new TreeMap<>();\n\n        // Lambda function equivalent to save_ratio\n        class SaveRatio {\n            void saveRatio(long a) {\n                long g2 = gcd(a, b);\n                double key = (double) Math.abs(u - a * z) / t;\n                result.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new TreeSet<>((p1, p2) -> {\n                    if (p1[1] != p2[1]) return Long.compare(p1[1], p2[1]);\n                    return Long.compare(p1[0], p2[0]);\n                })).add(new long[]{b / g2, a / g2});\n            }\n        }\n        SaveRatio saveRatio = new SaveRatio();\n\n        long b, c, z, t, u;\n        for (b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n            g = gcd(y, b);\n            c = b / g;\n            z = y / g;\n            t = b * z;\n            u = q * t + r * c;\n            saveRatio.saveRatio(u / z);\n\n            if (u % z != 0) {\n                saveRatio.saveRatio((u + z - 1) / z);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Get the first entry's first element\n        Map.Entry<Double, TreeSet<long[]>> firstEntry = result.firstEntry();\n        long[] p = firstEntry.getValue().first();\n\n        pw.println(p[1] + \"/\" + p[0]);\n        pw.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": 